cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Thinking Machines Atlas, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Thinking Machines Atlas: arguments for and against machine minds"
abstract: >-
  A teaching map of the debate over whether machines can think, understand,
  feel, act or matter morally: arguments for and against, in 11 clusters,
  with sources, responses and the relations between them, published as an
  interactive atlas and a workbook. Created and edited by Daniel Estrada (NJIT).
  Drafted and built with Claude (Anthropic); reviewed by AI models.
authors:
  - family-names: Estrada
    given-names: Daniel
    affiliation: New Jersey Institute of Technology
repository-code: "https://github.com/djestrada/Thinking-Machines-Atlas"
url: "https://djestrada.github.io/Thinking-Machines-Atlas/"
license:
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - philosophy of artificial intelligence
  - philosophy of mind
  - machine consciousness
  - Turing test
  - Chinese Room
  - large language models
  - AI moral status
  - open educational resource
